# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.egg-info/
.eggs/

# Virtual envs (not used per standing convention, but ignore defensively)
.venv/
venv/
env/

# OS/editor cruft
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp

# Anything that shouldn't ever end up inside core/ by accident — the real
# copies of these live as siblings of this folder (raid_system/db/,
# raid_system/logs/, raid_system/pass_raid_system.txt) and must never be
# committed here.
*.db
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
*.log
pass_raid_system.txt
.env

# Stray backup files left behind during editing (e.g. foo.html.bak.20260813) —
# never intentional commits, just editor/dev cruft.
*.bak
*.bak.*
*~

# Actual blog post content is runtime data (modules/blog.BLOGS_DIR is its
# source of truth on disk), not code — same "codebase vs. data" split as
# db/ living outside this repo entirely. Tracking these caused local test
# posts and production's real posts to diverge and fight each other across
# environments; keep the module directory itself (and its empty-dir
# behavior via BLOGS_DIR.mkdir(exist_ok=True) in code) but never the .md
# content inside it.
modules/blog/blogs/*.md
